Z||000000||V8Fiero||01-02-2001||11:22 PM||||Just wondering if my car insurance place is trying to screw me over. Ive been with the same car insurance place since 1986. Just a month or two ago my wife let the insurance expire on our van. Just got my fiero so no insurance on it yet. She went to the insurance agency to renew our policy and get insurance on my car. Well the agent said that we have to start over again since we dont or didnt have any insurance coverage when she walked into the office. It put me into a higher bracket and almost doubling my insurance. How can this be? Doesnt my history have any clought (sp?). HELP!!!!! Please, any advice would be appreciated.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||01-02-2001||11:39 PM||||I am not an agent, but have had some poor experiences lately with insurance and what I have found out is probably 90% of the time it is the local agent, not the company being a jacka$$. Try going to another agent with the same company and ask him about transferring your coverage to his office and see if he will cut you some slack.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||01-02-2001||11:45 PM||||Funny you should say that. I was thinking the same thing because my regular agent just quit and now some other guy is taking over for him......||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||01-02-2001||11:54 PM||||v8Fiero, I had to deal with that same thing just this summer. My Agent of 4 years(only been driving 4 years though) retired, and all of his clients were transferred to some money grabbing woman. She is polite and friendly, but she tried to grab another $20/month out of my pocket. I refused to make my next payment. She called, asked why I missed my first payment in 4 years(she had my records), and I said I wasn't going to pay more for the same coverage. A few days later, I recieved a new invoice in the mail for the "correct" amount, and it hasn't gone up yet. I'm pretty sure agents set their own rates. Money grabbing bas...||||reg||1
Z||000004||p4n1c||01-03-2001||09:14 AM||||According to my insurance agent that was a thing of the past, they usually let it slide for a couple months now if you let your insurance expire.  They are being really big pricks to you.<P>------------------<BR>p4n1c<BR>Come out swingin'||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-03-2001||10:30 AM||||We use to have one company for our insurance. The B*stards dropped us for 1 accident (wife driving) and 1 ticket (me driving). The accident wasn't even our fault (rear ended on a snowy day)and the other driver's insurance repaired our vehicle! (straighten bumper, and repaint) The ticket was a 52 in a 40 zone.<BR>They dropped us. We had to use a "fly-by-night" outfit for 6-months (super high rates) then we got our present carrier. Have been very happy since.<BR>We are paying less per month for 3 vehicles than we paid originally for 2 vehicles by the first company!<P>The first company was screwing people because they wanted to get out of the auto side of the insurance. From what I heard they screwed a lot of people. Now they want to get back into it. Guess who sent a letter to me? I sent a response back but geez I never heard if they liked it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||V8Fiero||01-03-2001||07:02 PM||||Well, after some "negotiating" with the agent today, and some minor threatening to go elsewhere, the SOB of an agent changed his tune and got me back down to where I should have been in the first place. Cut my rates in half. What a bunch of pricks these companies are.........Anyone wanna join the revolution against corporate america???? J/K<P>Just pisses me off though that they tried to stick it to me like that........<P>Thanks guys for all your input.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cheever2||01-03-2001||07:49 PM||||After 14 years with Nationwide, I was happy with a few minor incidents.  Then a year ago when I had my wreck, it was my first serious claim.  My problem was that I had to talk to about 9 different people before it was all taken care of.  It should not be that way; you should just have to call ONE person, and they take care of everything and get back to you.  I felt like I was not getting what I paid for: why should I be the middleman when they are the ones getting the big bucks?!  And that's my other problem, I think they're too expensive, although I never shopped around.  But now I will.<BR> <P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 01-03-2001).]||||reg||6
